L001179	For the asymptotic key rate over long distances, we consider the DI-QKD protocol studied in ~\cite{arnon2018practical, nadlinger2022experimental}  which does not contain the sifting procedure. By setting the ratio of Bell-test rounds as $\gamma=0.001$ (and a ratio $1-\gamma$ of the experimental rounds are all used to generate keys), we obtain the key rate against QBER and CHSH value, as shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:asymptotic}.
